      "text": "⚠️Heavy rainfall and blustery winds will continue over the northern Phillipines until mid Monday morning⚠️\n(11:00 Sun, Oct 19th, PHT) \nHazards: \n• Additional rainfall amounts ranging 50 to 100 mm, except 150 mm locally. \n• Winds gusting to 90km/h locally along the northeastern shores\n\nTropical storm Fengshen is currently located over Manila, Philippines and is bringing torrential rainfall to parts of the region. \nFengshen is forecast to travel northwest over the next 48 hours, emerging from the Philippines in 10 to 12 hours. \n\nThe system is expected to intensify considerably after leaving the Philippines, and is expected to max out in intensity late Tuesday as a T4 typhoon with sustained winds ranging 130 to 145km/h, well off-shore of Guangdong China. \nHowever, a powerful cold front will slam into the typhoon on Wednesday, pushing cold dry air into the core, which is expected to inevitably result in a weakening trend as the system veers southwest. \nThroughout the reminder of the week, Fengshen will travel southwest towards Vietnam, and is expected to weaken to a tropical storm or remnant low before making landfall. \n\nStay tuned for updates! \n#TyphoonFengshen #Tropicalstorm #Fengshen #Phillipines #Flooding",
